{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "logs": {
        "text": "php://stderr",
        "summary": "build/infection-summary.log"
    },
    "testFramework": "testo",
    // No "testFrameworkOptions": "--suite=Unit" here on purpose: Infection's
    // initial run must include tests/Integration/SqliteIntegrationTest, the
    // only #[Covers] source for DbUtmAttributionRepository and
    // M260801000000CreateUtmAttributionTable (ER-003, docs/evolved-rules.md).
    // Restricting to --suite=Unit later would silently zero out mutants for
    // both classes again while the reported MSI goes UP, not down.
    //
    // 94 stays honest at 96% Covered Code MSI (192 killed + 4 timed out of 204,
    // 2026-08-22 after exposing purgeBatchSize and bounding the malformed-row
    // report per call).
    // The four timeouts are the purge loop's two exit conditions: remove either
    // and the loop re-selects the same ids forever, which is exactly what the
    // veto-trigger test in SqliteIntegrationTest provokes. Eight escapes remain
    // and are all equivalent mutants, not test gaps:
    //   - DbUtmAttributionRepository::countByEntity (line 147) and
    //     countOlderThan (line 218), DecrementInteger on
    //     `max(0, (int) $count)` -> `max(-1, ...)`: $count comes from
    //     `Query::count()`, which vendor/yiisoft/db/src/Query/Query.php
    //     declares `@psalm-var non-negative-int|string` on the exact value
    //     this line casts — the domain the clamp defends against never
    //     contains a negative, so -1 and 0 clamp identically.
    //   - DbUtmAttributionRepository::deleteByEntity (line 157),
    //     DecrementInteger on `max(0, $affected)` -> `max(-1, ...)`:
    //     $affected is `AbstractCommand::execute()`'s result on a DELETE,
    //     which resolves to `PDOStatement::rowCount()` — per the PDO contract,
    //     rowCount() after a DELETE/UPDATE/INSERT is always >= 0. Same
    //     reasoning as above: the clamp's floor is never reached by -1 vs 0.
    //     purgeOlderThan() no longer clamps at all: its accumulator only ever
    //     adds a value the loop already proved positive.
    //   - DbUtmAttributionRepository::one() (line 238), IncrementInteger on
    //     `limit(1)` -> `limit(2)`: Query::one() always resolves through
    //     AbstractCommand::queryOne() (QUERY_MODE_ROW), which fetches exactly
    //     one row via a single PDO fetch() regardless of the SQL LIMIT value,
    //     as long as it is >= 1 — limit(1) and limit(2) produce an identical
    //     result row for any dataset.
    //   - UtmAttributionRowMapper::toRow() (lines 67, 68), NullSafePropertyCall
    //     on `$touchpoint->referrer?->url` / `?->host` -> `->url` / `->host`:
    //     verified empirically (PHP 8.5.6, this image) — reading a property on
    //     null through `->` (not `?->`) raises an E_WARNING and evaluates to
    //     `null`, the same value `?->` returns. The two forms are equivalent
    //     in observable value; they differ only in the warning, and this
    //     mutant survives specifically because nothing in this suite (or in
    //     testo's default config) promotes a PHP warning to a failure. A
    //     fail-on-warning mode, if ever added, would make this killable again.
    //   - UtmAttributionRowMapper::time() (line 261), GreaterThan and LogicalAnd
    //     around `getLastErrors()`: since PHP 8.2 a clean parse returns `false`,
    //     while an invalid calendar date returns an array with warning_count > 0.
    //     Both mutations therefore choose the same branch for every possible
    //     result of this API.
    "minMsi": 94,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    }
}
